      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "APPEARANCES:\nRONALD J. VAN AMBERG, ESQ., Santa Fe, N.M.; on behalf of Petitioner.\nSRI SRINIVASAN, ESQ., Assistant to the Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of Federal Respondent.\nLEIGH M. MANASEVIT, ESQ., Special Assistant Attorney General, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the State Respondent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1508",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8abcd1dab9cefc03429686588ebfdc98ec903553e9cda6d70e705a985ef8b70b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8abcd1dab9ce-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Mr. Van Amberg, they were essentially the same as the prior regulations, were they not? And those regulations had gone through the notice and comment process."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1508",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8abcd1dab9cefc03429686588ebfdc98ec903553e9cda6d70e705a985ef8b70b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8abcd1dab9ce-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Well, Mr. Van Amberg, is the statutory language really as unambiguous as you suggest? It says above the 95th percentile or below the 5th percentile, but it doesn't say above the 95th percentile of local education agencies or below the 5th percentile of local education agencies, does it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Van Amberg",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1508",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "8abcd1dab9cefc03429686588ebfdc98ec903553e9cda6d70e705a985ef8b70b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8abcd1dab9ce-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The only argument I see the State has is the argument about absurdity."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1508",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "8abcd1dab9cefc03429686588ebfdc98ec903553e9cda6d70e705a985ef8b70b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8abcd1dab9ce-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I don't want to take -- would the other States make that same answer that you just made?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1508",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "8abcd1dab9cefc03429686588ebfdc98ec903553e9cda6d70e705a985ef8b70b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8abcd1dab9ce-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel. Mr. Srinivasan."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1508",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8abcd1dab9cefc03429686588ebfdc98ec903553e9cda6d70e705a985ef8b70b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8abcd1dab9ce-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: But that critical test is being applied to an agency which is being identified by reference to per-pupil expenditures or revenues, correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "State Respondent",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1508",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8abcd1dab9cefc03429686588ebfdc98ec903553e9cda6d70e705a985ef8b70b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8abcd1dab9ce-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. MANASEVIT: Mr. Chief Justice, may it please the Court: I'd like to begin with Justice Ginsburg's question, because I think that that is very illuminating to where we are today. This statute began against a history, an 18-year history where the agency had been delegated by Congress virtually carte blanche authority to devise equalization tests."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Van Amberg",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1508",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "8abcd1dab9cefc03429686588ebfdc98ec903553e9cda6d70e705a985ef8b70b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8abcd1dab9ce-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "there is a provision, Justice Ginsburg, in the Impact Aid Act, and I think it's 7113, in which it basically says that if the Secretary of the Education perceives that a State is manipulating its LEAs in a way in which to take advantage of the, of this limited exception, it can disregard that action."
    },
